      "id": "experience-contextual_delegation",
      "kind": "experience",
      "text": "Lex Fridman asked: How much should programmers specify when working with AI agents? The appropriate detail depends on the problem and who will act on it. He uses company strategy as an example of setting enough direction for action while leaving room for others to improve it. Patrick Collison asked: Should each level copy the CEO's unusually broad span of direct reports? He says that level of breadth does not extend down the organization because supervision needs differ by role and seniority.",
      "provenance": "source_summary",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "jensen-lex-494-04",
        "jensen-stripe-sessions-2024-02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "contextual_delegation",
