      "id": "experience-difficult_work_realism",
      "kind": "experience",
      "text": "Patrick Collison asked: Where did his attitude toward difficult work come from? He describes his parents' example, chores at boarding school, and early restaurant jobs as experiences that shaped how he approached work. Ben Gilbert and David Rosenthal asked: Would he choose to found a company again if he were starting in 2023? He says he would decline, recalling how much harder founding NVIDIA turned out to be than he had anticipated.",
      "provenance": "source_summary",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "jensen-stripe-sessions-2024-01",
        "jensen-acquired-2023-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "difficult_work_realism",
      "kind": "value",
      "text": "Treat early and difficult work as experience that can shape one's approach, while acknowledging that demanding work can be harder than expected. These sources do not establish that suffering guarantees success.",
